3.2 Request Tracking

This functional area enables the AI Agent to retrieve access request information from MyIAM through secure, read-only APIs.

It supports two main use cases:

* Request Search: Retrieve access requests based on criteria such as requestor, requestee, application, entitlement, status and submission date.
* Request Details: Retrieve the detailed status, approval workflow and provisioning information of a specific access request.

The search capabilities previously defined as searchRequestsByUser, searchRequestsByAppEnt and searchRequestByStatus are consolidated into a single function, searchRequests, using optional input filters.

The API/backend layer is responsible for applying access controls and calculating consolidated business-level request statuses. The AI Agent uses the returned information to provide clear, contextual responses to end users.

3.2.1 searchRequests

Function Description

Returns a paginated list of access requests matching the specified filters.

The function supports searching by requestor, requestee, application, entitlement, request status and submission date. Multiple filters can be combined to narrow the results.

This function allows the AI Agent to answer natural-language questions about access requests without requiring separate API functions for each search criterion.

Agent Trigger

Use this function when the user asks to search, list or track access requests associated with a person, application, entitlement or status.

Examples:

* “Show me my pending requests.”
* “What requests did I submit for my team?”
* “Have I requested Bloomberg access?”
* “Show me my completed requests.”
* “What requests were submitted for Jean Dupont?”
* “Show me the pending requests for ServiceNow.”
* “Which requests were rejected last month?”

Endpoint

GET /api/v1/requests/search

Authentication and Authorization

Authentication is required. The API must determine the authenticated end-user identity from a trusted authentication context.

The authenticated user identity must not be supplied as an arbitrary query parameter by the AI Agent.

All search filters and returned results must be validated against the end user’s authorized access scope.

The intended access rules are:

User Role	Authorized Scope
Regular user	Own requests, whether requestor or requestee
Manager	Own requests and authorized team members’ requests
Administrator	Requests within the administrator’s authorized scope

The mechanism used to propagate the end-user identity when the Agent calls the API through a technical service account remains to be confirmed with the IAM and Innovation Lab development teams.

Input Parameters

Parameter	Type	Required	Description
requestorId	string	No	IIQ user ID of the person who submitted the request.
requesteeId	string	No	IIQ user ID of the beneficiary for whom the access was requested.
applicationName	string	No	Application name used to filter requests. Name resolution strategy to be confirmed.
entitlementName	string	No	Entitlement or role name used to filter requests. Name resolution strategy to be confirmed.
status	string	No	Business-level request status filter. Default: all. Accepted values and mapping to be validated.
scope	string	No	Requested search scope: me, my_team or all, subject to authorization. Default: me.
submittedAfter	date	No	ISO 8601 date. Returns requests submitted on or after this date.
submittedBefore	date	No	ISO 8601 date. Returns requests submitted on or before this date.
limit	integer	No	Maximum number of results returned. Default: 20. Maximum: 100.
offset	integer	No	Pagination offset. Default: 0.

Filter Combination Rules

* All supplied filters are combined using AND logic.
* requestorId and requesteeId can be used separately or together.
* applicationName and entitlementName can be used separately or together.
* If no user, application or entitlement filter is provided, the search defaults to the authenticated user’s authorized scope.
* The scope parameter cannot extend the caller’s authorized permissions.
* If submittedAfter and submittedBefore are both provided, the API returns requests within the specified submission date range.
* Pagination must be applied after filtering and authorization checks.

Request Status Handling

The status parameter represents a business-level filter, rather than the underlying IIQ technical status.

For the initial scope, the agreed priority filters are:

Input Status	Intended Meaning
pending	Requests that are still awaiting completion
completed	Requests that have successfully completed
cancelled	Requests that have been cancelled
all	All requests within the authorized scope

The final mapping between these business-level filters and IIQ internal statuses must be confirmed with the development team.

In particular, the handling of rejected requests and requests in execution must be explicitly defined to avoid incorrect classifications.

Response Schema

Field	Type	Description
totalCount	integer	Total number of matching requests after authorization and filtering, before pagination.
hasMore	boolean	Indicates whether additional results are available.
nextOffset	integer/null	Offset for retrieving the next page. Null when no additional results are available.
appliedFilters.requestorId	string/null	Resolved requestor filter applied to the search.
appliedFilters.requesteeId	string/null	Resolved requestee filter applied to the search.
appliedFilters.applicationName	string/null	Application filter applied.
appliedFilters.entitlementName	string/null	Entitlement filter applied.
appliedFilters.status	string	Normalized status filter applied.
appliedFilters.scope	string	Authorized scope applied to the search.
requests[].AccessRequestId	string	IIQ access request identifier.
requests[].globalStatus	string	Consolidated business-level request status calculated by the API/backend.
requests[].globalStatusLabel	string	Human-readable explanation of the overall request status.
requests[].RequestDate	datetime	UTC request submission timestamp.
requests[].requestor.UID	string	IIQ user ID of the requestor.
requests[].requestor.DisplayName	string	Full name of the requestor.
requests[].requestee.UID	string	IIQ user ID of the beneficiary.
requests[].requestee.DisplayName	string	Full name of the beneficiary.
requests[].items[].EntitlementName	string	Display name of the requested entitlement or role.
requests[].items[].Application	string	Application name in business terms.
requests[].items[].WorkItemStatus	string/null	Status of the individual request item, if available.
requests[].items[].WorkItemStatusLabel	string/null	Human-readable item-level status information, if available.

