Error Codes

HTTP Code	Description
400	Invalid or incompatible query parameters.
401	Missing, invalid or expired authentication token.
403	The caller is not authorized to access the requested scope or information.
500	Unexpected backend error.

A valid search returning no matching requests should normally return an empty requests array with totalCount set to 0, rather than an HTTP 404.

Implementation Notes

* The API/backend must enforce authorization independently of the AI Agent.
* The API/backend is responsible for calculating the consolidated globalStatus using predefined business rules.
* The Agent must not independently infer the authoritative Global Status from underlying technical statuses.
* The globalStatusLabel should provide meaningful business context, such as the current approval or provisioning stage, where available.
* Application and entitlement name resolution must be discussed with the Innovation Lab. The Agent may handle approximate or misspelled names before calling the API, but the final approach remains to be confirmed.
* If multiple application or entitlement matches are possible, the Agent should ask the user for clarification rather than selecting an uncertain match.
* Pagination must support limit and offset, with totalCount, hasMore and nextOffset returned consistently.
* The API must avoid exposing request information outside the authenticated user’s authorized scope.

3.2.2 getRequestDetails

Function Description

Returns detailed information about a specific access request, including its consolidated business-level status, requested application and entitlement, approval workflow and provisioning steps.

The function provides the information required to understand the current request status, identify pending approval or provisioning stages, and explain potential delays or rejection reasons.

Agent Trigger

Use this function when the user refers to a specific request ID or requests detailed information about a request previously identified through searchRequests.

Examples:

* “What is the status of REQ-2025-00145?”
* “Who still needs to approve my request?”
* “Why is my request still pending?”
* “Why was my request rejected?”
* “Show me all the approval steps for my request.”
* “Has the provisioning been completed?”

Endpoint

GET /api/v1/requests/{requestId}

Authentication and Authorization

Authentication is required.

The API must validate that the authenticated end user is authorized to view the specified request.

Access may be granted to the requestor, requestee, authorized manager or administrator according to the applicable MyIAM access-control rules.

The technical service account used for API connectivity must not automatically grant unrestricted access to request details.

Input Parameters

Parameter	Type	Required	Description
requestId	string	Yes	Unique IIQ access request identifier.

Response Schema

Field	Type	Description
AccessRequestId	string	Unique access request identifier.
globalStatus	string	Consolidated business-level status calculated by the API/backend.
globalStatusLabel	string	Human-readable explanation of the overall status.
RequestDate	datetime	UTC submission timestamp.
requestedBy.DisplayName	string	Full name of the requestor.
requestedFor.DisplayName	string	Full name of the beneficiary.
items[].EntitlementName	string	Requested entitlement or role.
items[].Application	string	Application name.
items[].EntitlementType	string	Entitlement or business role type.
items[].provisioningType	string	CONNECTED or MANUAL.
items[].approvalSteps[].stepOrder	integer	Position of the approval step in the workflow.
items[].approvalSteps[].stepName	string	Business name of the approval step.
items[].approvalSteps[].status	string	Current status of the approval step.
items[].approvalSteps[].approver.displayName	string/null	Name of the assigned approver, if available.
items[].approvalSteps[].approver.jobTitle	string/null	Job title of the approver, if available.
items[].approvalSteps[].decisionDate	datetime/null	Timestamp of the approval decision, if available.
items[].approvalSteps[].comment	string/null	Approval or rejection comment, if available.
items[].approvalSteps[].isOverdue	boolean/null	Whether the step has exceeded its applicable SLA, if determinable.
items[].provisioningSteps[].stepName	string	Name of the provisioning step.
items[].provisioningSteps[].status	string	Current provisioning status.
items[].provisioningSteps[].completedAt	datetime/null	Provisioning completion timestamp, if available.
items[].provisioningSteps[].adminTeam	string/null	Responsible administration team for manual provisioning, if available.

Global Status Calculation

The globalStatus represents the consolidated business-level status of the entire access request.

It must be calculated by the API/backend using predefined business rules derived from the relevant underlying approval, provisioning and work item statuses.

The AI Agent must not independently determine the authoritative request status by aggregating these technical statuses.

The API should return a consistent status and an associated human-readable explanation.

The detailed mapping and aggregation rules must be defined and validated with the MyIAM development team.

